docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T13.log:4192:docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/00-decompose.log:788:{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_013zgGbBpL5RCG9X6xGX3GFk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LLzhtrw7NNpnBWtrst5QqD","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T36.md","content":"# T36 — Phase 5 — MCP surface for working memory inspection + event capture for include/exclude reasons\n\n**Phase:** 5\n**Type:** backend\n**Model class:** balanced\n**Depends on:** T34, T35\n**Spec anchor:** [§Phase 5: Working Memory](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-5-working-memory), [§5. Working Memory](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#5-working-memory), [§3. Event Log](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#3-event-log), [§9. MCP Surface](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#9-mcp-surface)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard (`/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md`); Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Goal\n\nThis task delivers the MCP tool that lets a client inspect the current `WorkingMemoryState` and the event-capture hooks that automatically log included and excluded context per spec §Phase 5 deliverable (\"automatic event capture for included and excluded context\"). The MCP tool exposes the same compact-by-default shape the rest of the MCP surface uses; the event hooks emit `MemoryRetrieved` and `MemoryExpanded` events (Phase 2 event kinds) every time the working memory's `selected_memories` or `excluded_memories` change. Together these make working memory observable — meeting the Phase 5 Definition of Done (\"workflow tools can show what context is active, why it is active, and what was intentionally excluded\").\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n\n> \"Phase 5: Working Memory — Deliverables: ... MCP surface for inspecting current working memory; automatic event capture for included and excluded context ...\" (spec §Phase 5: Working Memory)\n\n> \"Required event types: ... ContextBundleReturned; MemoryRetrieved; MemoryExpanded ...\" (spec §3. Event Log)\n\n> \"Definition of done: workflow tools can show what context is active, why it is active, and what was intentionally excluded; context management is no longer just prompt accumulation.\" (spec §Phase 5: Working Memory)\n\n> \"Every tool response should support: compact rendering; full structured JSON; context handles; stable expansion targets; budget controls.\" (spec §9. MCP Surface)\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs:\n  - T34 `WorkingMemoryState` and checkpoint API.\n  - T35 `OpContext`, eight operations, and `record_state_mutation` internal hook.\n  - Phase 2 event-log API — exposes `MemoryRetrieved`, `MemoryExpanded`, `ContextBundleReturned` writers.\n- Existing files in the repo this task builds on:\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/server.rs` — JSON-RPC server registration.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` — `McpHandler::handle_tools_call()` dispatch and tool-schema declarations.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/context_cache.rs` — context-handle convention for round-trippable handles.\n  - Phase 2 event writer (assumed to live at `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/events/`).\n- Standards files to honor: `/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md` (file ≤800 lines, single source of truth — reuse the existing MCP dispatch convention); `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md` (compact-by-default; build/deploy procedure for the daemon).\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Re-read spec §Phase 5 deliverables, §3. Event Log event-kind list, and §9. MCP Surface response contract to fix the tool shape and event-emission contract.\n2. Implement `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/working_memory_tool.rs`: register a new MCP tool `inspect_working_memory` with schema `{ task_id: string, mode: \"compact\" | \"diagnostic\", include_excluded: boolean }`. The handler loads the active `WorkingMemoryState` for the task (from the session-scoped in-memory store maintained by T35's `OpContext`, falling back to the latest checkpoint if the session has rolled), then returns either a compact summary (via T35 `summarize`) or the full state including `excluded_memories` when `include_excluded=true`. Response carries an `expansion_handle` per spec §9 so the caller can expand the full state without re-fetching.\n3. Wire the tool into `mcp.rs` dispatch alongside the existing 43 tools. Tool registration includes the schema in the MCP `tools/list` response; failure to expose a parameter is a contract violation caught by the cross-layer MCP schema test gate.\n4. Implement `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/event_hooks.rs`: a small module exposing `emit_memory_retrieved(state_before, state_after, op_summary, writer)` and `emit_memory_expanded(state_before, state_after, op_summary, writer)`. Each function computes the diff (which identities were added to `selected_memories`, which were added to `excluded_memories` with reasons), packages the diff into an event payload per Phase 2's event-payload contract (workspace, branch, session, task, actor, timestamp, payload hash, compact summary, optional full payload location), and writes through the Phase 2 event writer.\n5. Attach the hooks to T35's `record_state_mutation` so every state-mutating operation emits the appropriate event automatically: `retrieve` and `compress` emit `MemoryRetrieved` (since they decide what is included/excluded); `expand` emits `MemoryExpanded`; `pin`, `evict`, `filter`, `checkpoint` emit `MemoryRetrieved` when they change inclusion/exclusion. `summarize` emits no event.\n6. Honor the spec invariant \"the full event stream should not be injected into prompts\" — the event hooks never put event data back into `WorkingMemoryState`. Events flow one way: state mutation → event log.\n7. Hot-path discipline: event writes share the existing Phase 2 write budget (`≤5ms P99`). If the writer returns a backpressure error, the operation does not fail — the event is dropped with a `warn!` log naming the task and operation, per `coding.md` \"no silent .catch\" but tolerant of event-log overload.\n8. Add `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/working_memory_tool_tests.rs` covering: tool registration appears in `tools/list`; compact mode returns a summary; diagnostic mode returns the full state and embedded `RetrievalBundle`-shaped `selected_memories`; `include_excluded=true` returns excluded entries with reasons; expansion handle round-trips back to the same state; a synthetic event writer captures one `MemoryRetrieved` event per `retrieve` call and one `MemoryExpanded` event per `expand` call; event payload carries the included and excluded identity diffs and reasons.\n9. Run `cd daemon && cargo build --release` (release build verifies the whole daemon still compiles with the new tool registered), then `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-daemon --lib rpc::working_memory_tool_tests`. Deploy the new daemon binary per the project rule (`pkill -f lattice && cp daemon/target/release/lattice extension/bin/ && cp daemon/target/release/lattice ~/.vscode/extensions/lattice.lattice-0.1.0/bin/`) only when explicitly told to ship; the test commands themselves do not require a redeploy.\n\n## Files expected\n\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/working_memory_tool.rs` — MCP tool registration, schema, handler, dispatch wiring.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/event_hooks.rs` — `emit_memory_retrieved`, `emit_memory_expanded`, state-diff computation, event payload assembly.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/working_memory_tool_tests.rs` — in-tree tests for tool registration, compact/diagnostic modes, exclude visibility, expansion handle, event capture.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/working_memory_tool.rs`\n- `cd daemon && cargo build --release`\n- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-daemon --lib rpc::working_memory_tool_tests`\n\n## Coding-standard checks\n\n- File length ≤800 lines per file.\n- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10. The MCP handler decomposes mode handling into helpers; event-diff computation is its own function.\n- Schema parity: the MCP tool JSON schema mirrors the Rust handler's parameter struct exactly; the response shape mirrors `WorkingMemoryState` (compact view exposes a documented subset). Schema declaration and Rust struct are updated in the same commit.\n- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code, or unjustified `#[allow(...)]`.\n- Single source of truth: state loading uses T34's `load_checkpoint` / T35's `OpContext` session store; no parallel state lookup. Event writing uses the Phase 2 event writer; no parallel event payload assembler.\n- No broken windows: dead imports removed; the backpressure-drop path logs at `warn!` with task and operation context, never silent.\n- Doc citation: tool comments cite `## 9. MCP Surface`; event-hook comments cite `## 3. Event Log` and `## Phase 5: Working Memory` per `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Every file in \"Files expected\" exists with real content (no stubs).\n- [ ] Every verification command in tasks.json passes from repo root.\n- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n- [ ] No deferred work: tool registration, compact/diagnostic modes, exclude visibility, expansion handle, automatic event capture all delivered in this task.\n- [ ] Every Phase-5 state mutation emits an event without manual call sites — the `record_state_mutation` hook is the single attachment point.\n- [ ] Backpressure on the event log degrades to a logged drop, not a failed operation.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3458,"cache_read_input_tokens":74783,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3458,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":51,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_019RjXwCuf57BAKn88mWkE24","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"4430d74f-dcef-44ba-9df8-04d1b33b60f6","request_id":"req_011Cb7NHj1kpRYTTxArY2nhh","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write Phase 4+5 task briefs"}
