cerpts that drive this task\n\n> 1-3 direct quotes from the spec sections that bind this task.\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs (list prior task artifacts).\n- Existing repo files this task builds on (e.g. `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory/store.rs` for memory; `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/storage/` for SQLite patterns; `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` for tool dispatch).\n- Standards to honor.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. ... concrete step\n... 5-10 steps. For schema tasks, list the table columns explicitly per spec. For writer/reader API tasks, list the function signatures. For event capture wiring, name the workflow tools to instrument.\n\n## Files expected\n\nFor each path in tasks.json: `path` — one-line purpose.\n\n## Verification\n\nList each command verbatim with a one-sentence pass-criterion.\n\n## Coding-standard checks\n\n- File length ≤800 lines.\n- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10.\n- Schema parity (every non-private column has a schema field; nullability matches).\n- No silent error handling — every `Result` checked or annotated.\n- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, commented-out code.\n- For SQLite: wrap raw SQL in `rusqlite::params!` or equivalent; never string-format SQL.\n- Use `tracing` for observability (project convention).\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Every file in \"Files expected\" exists with real content.\n- [ ] Every verification command passes from repo root.\n- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n- [ ] No deferred work: spec items for this phase done in this task or a sibling task in the same phase.\n- [ ] Architecture doc updated in the same task if behavior is publicly observable.\n```\n\n**For review files (R18, R25, R26), use this template:**\n\n```\n# <REVIEW_ID> — <Title>\n\n**Phase:** Review for Phase <N> | Contract gate\n**Type:** review\n**Model class:** advanced\n**Depends on:** <list>\n**Spec anchor:** [§<section>](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#<anchor>)\n\n## Purpose\n\nWhat this review certifies. For R26 (contract gate), explicitly call out that this gate certifies cross-layer round-trip contracts.\n\n## Inputs to read\n\n- Every artifact from dependency tasks.\n- Spec sections claimed satisfied.\n- Standards relevant to this phase.\n\n## Review procedure\n\n1. ... step\n... 5-10 steps. For R26 specifically, the procedure includes:\n- Verify identity references serialize cleanly into event payloads.\n- Verify event payloads round-trip back to identity targets.\n- Verify memory links reference stable identities not transient names.\n- Run `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib contract_tests::identity_event_memory`.\n\n## Required sections in the review output file\n\n`docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/<REVIEW_ID>-<slug>.md` with these mandatory headings:\n\n(For R18 and R25):\n- `## Spec alignment`\n- `## Coding-standard alignment`\n- `## P99 budget evidence` (R18 only; per Phase 2 DoD)\n- `## CounterMemory coverage` (R25 only)\n- `## Findings`\n- `## Verdict`\n\n(For R26 contract gate):\n- `## Contract surfaces` — name every cross-layer surface this gate covers.\n- `## Round-trip evidence` — for each surface, the test that proves the round-trip.\n- `## Schema regression coverage` — confirm no schema drift between layers.\n- `## Findings`\n- `## Verdict`\n\n## Verification\n\nList commands from tasks.json verbatim with pass criteria.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Review markdown file exists.\n- [ ] Every required section present with concrete content.\n- [ ] Contract tests added (R26 only) and passing.\n- [ ] Verdict declared.\n```\n\n**Task-specific content guidance:**\n\n- T11 — event kinds: list all 20 from spec §Event Log (`AssistantTaskStarted`, `ToolCalled`, `ToolResult`, `ContextBundleReturned`, `MemoryRetrieved`, `MemoryExpanded`, `PlanCreated`, `FileRead`, `PatchApplied`, `TestRunStarted`, `TestRunCompleted`, `DiagnosticObserved`, `UserCorrection`, `UserPreferenceObserved`, `WorkflowSucceeded`, `WorkflowFailed`, `MemoryCreated`, `MemoryUpdated`, `MemoryInvalidated`, `MemoryConsolidated`). Each carries workspace id, branch, session id, task id, actor, timestamp, stable references, payload hash, compact summary, optional full payload location.\n- T12 — SQLite tables: `events`, `event_payloads` (spillover). Indexes: task/session/workspace/branch.\n- T13 — writer API: bound P99 ≤5ms on hot path, payload hashing, spillover for large payloads.\n- T14 — reader API: filter by task/session/workspace/branch with bounded result sets.\n- T15 — wire event capture into prepare_change, plan_edit, get_context_capsule, expand_context, get_working_set_context, trace_scenario, summarize_subsystem, impact_from_diff, diagnose_failure, record_workflow_outcome, save_observation, etc.\n- T16 — compaction must be daemon-managed background operation (spec §Storage Design \"Event log compaction\"). Snapshot format versioned and independently readable. Architecture doc required.\n- T17 — tests for ordering, replay, corruption, scoping, P99 budget. Use `--include-ignored` for budget tests.\n- T19 — memory schema redesign: all required fields from spec §Memory Graph (stable id, content, class, assertion type, scope, verification status, confidence + reason, freshness policy, validity conditions, invalidation triggers, provenance events, evidence references, linked files/symbols/docs/tests/memories, contradiction/supersession links, access history, usefulness scores, last verified state). Classes include CounterMemory.\n- T20 — first-class link records (source, target, link type, strength, reason, evidence event, created_by, created_at, verification_status). Link types: supports/contradicts/supersedes/refines/generalizes/specializes/co_occurs_with/derived_from/applies_to/validated_by/invalidated_by.\n- T21 — streams from spec §ViLoMem (code topology, workflow episodes, failure patterns, semantic repo claims, architecture decisions, user/team preferences, docs and contract state). Scope: session, branch, repo, user, organization.\n- T22 — migration from existing `memories` table. Architecture doc required.\n- T23 — CRUD + verification status transitions (unverified → in_review → verified, plus stale/contradicted/superseded/expired/invalidated).\n- T24 — tests for contradiction, supersession, replay.\n- R18 reviews Phase 2 (event log) with P99 evidence; R25 reviews Phase 3 (memory graph) with CounterMemory coverage; R26 is the contract gate for Identity ↔ Event ↔ Memory.\n\nRead the spec yourself for the exact section text and quote it. Cite spec headings precisely.\n\nWrite all 16 files, then report file count + first 3 paths confirmed via ls. Do NOT modify tasks.json, context.md, or plan.md. Do NOT implement any code.","uuid":"98c92ff6-2197-409c-8acf-c7d582b71485","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768"}
