": consolidate `propose_memory_evolution` + `apply_memory_evolution` into one tool with `action` parameter).\n- T59 — new memory tools: `verify_memory` + `explain_memory` (unified per spec §MCP Surface discipline), `list_memory_conflicts`.\n- T60 — new tools: `consolidate_session`, `get_memory_metrics`, `get_event_trace`.\n- T61 — tool surface audit doc + final MCP reference. Required headings: `## Final tool list`, `## Audit findings`, `## Collapsed tools`. Documents which tools were collapsed and why per spec §Phase 8 \"Tool surface discipline\".\n- T62 — workflow outcome recording integrated by default + composition tests.\n- R63 — Phase 8 review. Required headings: `## Spec alignment`, `## Coding-standard alignment`, `## Tool-surface size`, `## Findings`, `## Verdict`.\n- R64 — contract gate MCP schema regression. Required headings: `## Schema surfaces`, `## Render-mode coverage` (compact/full/diagnostic/handles for every tool), `## Backward-compatibility shims`, `## Findings`, `## Verdict`. New test file `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp_schema_tests.rs`.\n- T65 — metric collection: all required signals from spec §Phase 9 \"Required metrics\": tool calls per successful task, irrelevant files opened per task, relevant anchor recall, memory inclusion precision, memory later-used rate, stale memory surfaced rate, contradiction missed rate, tests recommended vs needed, workflow success after first plan.\n- T66 — benchmark task fixture repository: cross-language (Rust, TypeScript, Python). Golden anchors JSON per spec §Risks \"Overfitting To Current Repo\" control.\n- T67 — `get_memory_metrics` + retrieval relevance surfaces wired through MCP.\n- T68 — regression dashboard CLI (`lattice_report` binary) + architecture doc.\n- T69 — metrics regression coverage tests asserting spec §Measurable Success Criteria initial targets: 30% fewer discovery calls, 40% fewer irrelevant reads, 80% memory precision, zero trusted display of stale/contradicted, 90% correct relevant-test recommendation.\n- R70 — Phase 9 review. Required headings: `## Spec alignment`, `## Coding-standard alignment`, `## Success-criteria coverage`, `## Findings`, `## Verdict`.\n\nRead the spec yourself for exact text. Quote it.\n\nFor each task: 5-10 concrete steps, exact file paths from tasks.json, exact verification commands from tasks.json. Coding-standard checks must include file ≤800 lines, function ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, schema parity, no broken windows.\n\nWrite all 15 files, then report file count + first 3 paths confirmed. Do NOT modify tasks.json, context.md, or plan.md. Do NOT implement any code.","uuid":"34b8629a-7137-41b6-b6b2-4a34f4add741","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768"}
