docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T04.log:2700:./docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/00-decompose.log:579:{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01NueXwL9yjYjF3Xf5Rf944S","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01X3nysjq6XjQ3Lv3FVUUyCV","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"grep -n '\"id\":' /home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks.json | head -100","description":"Find task IDs in tasks.json"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6432,"cache_read_input_tokens":39588,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6432,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01XjrTa6YAS1dmMW989ZPauZ","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"b3769531-9304-4844-8644-db5e11ee5960","request_id":"req_011Cb7Mn8KP4J6uuZu9ypPDc","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write Phase 10+11+Final task briefs"}
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T04.log:2701:./docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/00-decompose.log:582:{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_013ZXuTanJH7X6D7LHKK4aiQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01S3ci1mH34uJkBZ1KSiAPE5","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T04.md","content":"# T04 — Phase 0 — Baseline benchmark capture (current Lattice workflows)\n\n**Phase:** 0\n**Type:** tests\n**Model class:** balanced\n**Depends on:** T01\n**Spec anchor:** [§Phase 0: Fork Foundation](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-0-fork-foundation)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard; Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Goal\n\nThis task captures benchmark numbers for the existing Lattice workflow tools so Phase 4 (retrieval), Phase 9 (metrics), and the hot-path budget assertions in Phase 1 and Phase 2 have a real baseline to regress against. Spec §Phase 0 Deliverables explicitly requires \"baseline benchmark suite from current Lattice workflows.\" Without these numbers, later claims of \"no regression\" or \"30 percent fewer discovery tool calls\" cannot be evaluated objectively. The benchmark must follow Rust criterion conventions, run from `cargo bench`, and emit a JSON metrics file the build harness can verify.\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n\n> \"Phase 0 Deliverables: ... baseline benchmark suite from current Lattice workflows.\"\n\n> \"Verification: current Lattice daemon tests pass in the fork before major changes; current MCP workflow fixtures run unchanged or with documented compatibility shims.\"\n\n> Spec §Measurable Success Criteria targets (\"30 percent fewer discovery tool calls on benchmark tasks; 40 percent fewer irrelevant file reads\") only make sense against a measured baseline.\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs: `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-fork-or-extend-decision.md` from T01 (confirms the branch where baselines are captured).\n- Existing files in the repo this task builds on:\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/intelligence/benchmark_tests.rs` (existing in-tree benchmarks)\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/query/benchmark_tests.rs`\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/intelligence/` (workflow tools: `prepare_change`, `get_context_capsule`, `plan_edit`, `expand_context`, `get_working_set_context`, `trace_scenario`, `impact_from_diff`, `diagnose_failure`)\n  - `daemon/Cargo.toml` workspace (must add `criterion` as a `[dev-dependencies]` entry if not already present)\n- Standards files to honor: `coding.md` (tests as documentation, file ≤800 lines, no broken windows); `AGENTS.md` (do not introduce regressions while measuring baselines).\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Read T01 to confirm the branch and `daemon/crates/lattice-core/Cargo.toml` to confirm criterion availability; add `criterion = { version = \"...\", features = [\"html_reports\"] }` under `[dev-dependencies]` and a `[[bench]]` entry pointing at the new file if needed.\n2. Create `daemon/crates/lattice-core/benches/baseline_workflows.rs` using `criterion::{criterion_group, criterion_main, Criterion}`.\n3. Add one benchmark function per critical workflow: `bench_prepare_change`, `bench_get_context_capsule`, `bench_expand_context`, `bench_impact_from_diff`, `bench_diagnose_failure`, `bench_search_symbols`, `bench_find_relevant_tests`. Each must operate on a fixture workspace identical to the one used in `benchmark_tests.rs` so future regressions are comparable.\n4. Each benchmark records latency distribution (p50, p95, p99) and result-size statistics (bytes returned, candidate count). The fixture must be deterministic and self-contained — no I/O outside a tempdir.\n5. After running, persist a structured metrics snapshot to `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/baselines/baseline_metrics.json` containing one object per benchmark with `name`, `p50_us`, `p95_us`, `p99_us`, `bytes_returned`, `commit_sha`, and `recorded_at`. A small helper in the bench file or a follow-up `bench_report` binary should write this file at the end of the bench run.\n6. Add `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/baselines/README.md` explaining how to re-run the benchmarks, how to interpret the metrics file, and the rule that regression checks in Phase 4 and Phase 9 use this file as the reference.\n7. Document the absolute target budgets (≤2ms P99 identity resolution, ≤5ms P99 event write on hot paths) and confirm the bench file measures the pre-Phase-1 baseline so the budget asserts can be evaluated as deltas.\n8. Run `cd daemon && cargo build --release --benches` and `cd daemon && cargo bench --bench baseline_workflows -- --warm-up-time 1 --measurement-time 3` to validate the bench compiles, runs, and produces the metrics file.\n\n## Files expected\n\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/benches/baseline_workflows.rs` — criterion benchmarks for the eight critical pre-fork workflows; deterministic fixture; writes structured metrics snapshot at the end of the run.\n- `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/baselines/baseline_metrics.json` — machine-readable baseline numbers used by Phase 4 and Phase 9 regression checks.\n- `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/baselines/README.md` — operator-facing description of how the baseline is captured, refreshed, and consumed.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/benches/baseline_workflows.rs` — confirms the criterion bench file exists.\n- `test -f docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/baselines/baseline_metrics.json` — confirms the metrics snapshot exists in the build directory.\n- `cd daemon && cargo build --release --benches` — confirms the bench compiles in release profile without warnings the task introduced.\n- `cd daemon && cargo bench --bench baseline_workflows -- --warm-up-time 1 --measurement-time 3` — confirms the bench runs end-to-end and emits criterion output; passing means the metrics file is regenerated on each run.\n\n## Coding-standard checks\n\n- File length ≤800 lines (verify with `wc -l daemon/crates/lattice-core/benches/baseline_workflows.rs`).\n- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10 — every bench function and helper must fit.\n- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code.\n- No unjustified `// allow(...)` or suppressions.\n- Public API names follow intent-over-mechanism naming (e.g. `bench_prepare_change`, not `bench_test_1`).\n- For schema changes: not applicable.\n- Doc citation: cite the exact `## Phase 0: Fork Foundation` heading from the spec and `## Measurable Success Criteria` in the README so the link between baselines and later targets is explicit.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Every file in \"Files expected\" exists with real content (no stubs).\n- [ ] Every verification command in tasks.json passes from repo root.\n- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n- [ ] No deferred work: no item from spec §Phase 0 punted to a later phase.\n- [ ] If a backward-incompatible change was needed, the AGENTS.md \"Backward-compatibility and contract discipline\" section was followed and the architecture doc was updated in the same task.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":615,"cache_read_input_tokens":49571,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":615,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_016juPk15H1M5x3FpzubRVsP","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"e72ead94-6991-45f3-9e11-4b9d4e5b3068","request_id":"req_011Cb7Mcwaxi2NndD8b7oC78","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write Phase 0+1 task briefs"}
