ork-build/tasks/<TASK_ID>.md`:\n\nT27, T28, T29, T30, T31, T32, R33, T34, T35, T36, T37, R38\n\n**Use the same template structure as the prior agents** (Goal, Spec excerpts, Inputs, Steps, Files expected, Verification, Coding-standard checks, Definition of done) for work tasks; for review tasks use the review template with required headings.\n\n**Task-specific guidance:**\n\n- T27 — intent classifier: classify user task by type (debug/refactor/explain/add-feature/test/docs/migration/etc.). Should be feature-based and inspectable per spec §Ranking Complexity risk.\n- T28 — anchor extractor: extract paths, symbols, errors, commands, APIs, config keys; resolve into graph identities using identity resolver from Phase 1.\n- T29 — hybrid candidate retrieval: exact path/symbol lookup + code graph traversal + doc backlinks/outgoing links + FTS + embeddings + event similarity + memory links + workflow similarity + recent working memory.\n- T30 — scoring with ALL signals from spec §Retrieval Engine \"Ranking signals\": task-type compatibility, graph proximity, exact identifier match, semantic similarity, verification status, freshness, scope, evidence strength, contradiction/supersession state, past usefulness, recent successful reuse, user preference compatibility, token cost. Diagnostic mode exposes scores AND reasons.\n- T31 — compact response shaper: every result has an `inclusion_reason` and an `expansion_handle`. Forward-compatible with Phase 5 working memory checkpoints per spec §Phase 4 scope constraint.\n- T32 — benchmark suite + golden anchors + ranking regression tests.\n- R33 — Phase 4 review. Required headings: `## Spec alignment`, `## Coding-standard alignment`, `## Inclusion-reason discipline`, `## Findings`, `## Verdict`.\n- T34 — working memory state from spec §Working Memory: task statement, interpreted intent, active files/symbols, active hypotheses, active failures, current plan, selected memories, excluded memories and reasons, budget decisions, unresolved questions, verification status. Table: `working_memory_checkpoints`.\n- T35 — operations: retrieve, summarize, filter, pin, evict, expand, compress, checkpoint.\n- T36 — MCP tool for inspection + event capture for include/exclude reasons (`MemoryRetrieved`, `MemoryExpanded` events from Phase 2).\n- T37 — tests: budgets, pinned context, eviction, checkpoint restore.\n- R38 — Phase 5 review. Required headings: `## Spec alignment`, `## Coding-standard alignment`, `## Excluded-context auditability`, `## Findings`, `## Verdict`.\n\nRead the spec yourself for exact section text and quote it. Cite spec headings precisely.\n\nFor each task, include 5-10 concrete steps, exact file paths (from tasks.json `files_expected`), and the exact verification commands from tasks.json. The \"Coding-standard checks\" section should include: file ≤800 lines, function ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, schema parity for SQL tasks, no broken windows.\n\nWrite all 12 files, then report file count + first 3 paths confirmed. Do NOT modify tasks.json, context.md, or plan.md. Do NOT implement any code.","agentId":"a8b9cf908dfeed8f7","agentType":"general-purpose","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 12 task brief files written successfully.\n\n**Files written: 12**\n\n**First 3 paths confirmed:**\n- `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T27.md` (intent classifier)\n- `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T28.md` (anchor extractor + resolver)\n- `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T29.md` (hybrid candidate retrieval)\n\n**All 12 files:** T27, T28, T29, T30, T31, T32, R33, T34, T35, T36, T37, R38.\n\n**Coverage summary:**\n- **Phase 4 (T27–T32, R33):** Intent classifier with feature-based ranker per §Ranking Complexity; anchor extractor for all 6 spec-named types (paths/symbols/errors/commands/APIs/config keys) routing through Phase 1 IdentityResolver; hybrid candidate retrieval covering all 9 spec-named sources with budget enforcement; scorer implementing every one of the 13 spec-named ranking signals with diagnostic mode; compact shaper with non-optional `inclusion_reason` and `expansion_handle` plus Phase 5 forward-compatibility contract; benchmark + golden anchors + ranking regression tests writing baseline JSON; review with required headings `## Spec alignment`, `## Coding-standard alignment`, `## Inclusion-reason discipline`, `## Findings`, `## Verdict`.\n- **Phase 5 (T34–T37, R38):** `WorkingMemoryState` carrying all 11 spec-named fields plus typed `ExcludedMemory.exclusion_reason`; `working_memory_checkpoints` table with versioned schema and SHA-256 hash; all 8 spec-named operations (retrieve/summarize/filter/pin/evict/expand/compress/checkpoint) with idempotency and pin-protection contracts; MCP `inspect_working_memory` tool plus automatic event capture wiring `MemoryRetrieved`/`MemoryExpanded` events from Phase 2; 4 test families (budgets/pins/eviction/checkpoint restore); review with required headings `## Spec alignment`, `## Coding-standard alignment`, `## Excluded-context auditability`, `## Findings`, `## Verdict`.\n\nEvery brief uses the T01 template (Goal, Spec excerpts, Inputs, Steps, Files expected, Verification, Coding-standard checks, Definition of done), quotes the exact spec headings verbatim, lists 7–10 concrete steps, names the exact file paths from `tasks.json` `files_expected`, copies the exact `verification_commands` from `tasks.json`, and includes the requested coding-standard items (file ≤800 lines, function ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, schema parity for the SQL task T34, no broken windows). No tasks.json, context.md, plan.md, or implementation code was modified."}],"totalDurationMs":647944,"totalTokens":90189,"totalToolUseCount":30,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":416,"cache_read_input_tokens":88692,"output_tokens":1080,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_reques