ines, nesting ≤3, schema parity, no broken windows.\n\nWrite all 15 files, then report file count + first 3 paths confirmed. Do NOT modify tasks.json, context.md, or plan.md. Do NOT implement any code.","agentId":"a59164d0498b3e0b7","agentType":"general-purpose","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 15 target files are present (T56, T57, T58, T59, T60, T61, T62, R63, R64, T65, T66, T67, T68, T69, R70).\n\nReport:\n\nFiles written: 15\n\nFirst 3 paths confirmed:\n- /home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T56.md\n- /home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T57.md\n- /home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T58.md\n\nKey drafting notes:\n\n- T56–T57 ground the Phase 8 redesigned workflow tools in spec §Phase 8 deliverables (\"one-call edit-planning bundles,\" \"compact by default with deliberate expansion handles\") and explicitly compose Phase 1 identity, Phase 2 event log, Phase 3 memory graph, Phase 4 retrieval, Phase 5 working memory, and Phase 7 verification.\n- T58 / T59 carry the spec §MCP Surface \"Tool surface discipline\" collapse directives verbatim, shipping unified `propose_memory_evolution(action=propose|apply|reject)` and `verify_explain_memory(mode=verify|explain|verify_and_explain)` with deprecation shims per T02 compatibility policy.\n- T60 ships `consolidate_session` (proposal-only writes per spec §Consolidation Engine), `get_memory_metrics` (honest `null` over fabricated zeros), and `get_event_trace` (workspace-bounded).\n- T61 has the required `## Final tool list`, `## Audit findings`, `## Collapsed tools` headings plus a `## Decisions not to collapse` section to document rationale.\n- T62 wires `WorkflowOutcomeRecorder` by default into every T56–T60 tool and asserts the spec §Phase 2 ≤5ms P99 hot-path budget.\n- R63 includes required `## Spec alignment`, `## Coding-standard alignment`, `## Tool-surface size`, `## Find