n- Status badges + loading + empty + error states for every interactive surface.\n\n**Task-specific guidance:**\n\n- T71 — extension review-panel scaffolding: register a new webview view contribution under existing `viewsContainers.activitybar.lattice` in `extension/package.json`. RPC bridge translates tool responses into typed UI state. Set up i18n with at least `en.json`.\n- T72 — memory inbox: list view with filters (status, scope, class), status badges (verified/unverified/in_review/stale/contradicted/superseded/expired/invalidated).\n- T73 — promotion queue + contradiction queue with accept/reject. Dialogs are native `<dialog>` per ui-specification.md.\n- T74 — stale memory view + evidence inspector + verification trigger that calls `verify_memory` (new tool from Phase 8).\n- T75 — event trace view + retrieval explanation view (shows ranking scores + reasons from Phase 4 diagnostic mode).\n- T76 — consolidation queue + indexing health + workspace graph health.\n- T77 — extension UI smoke tests via VS Code test runner (`npm test` → `node ./out/test/runTest.js`). Tests cover at least: extension activates, review panel registers, each subview renders without throwing.\n- R78 — Phase 10 review. Required headings: `## Spec alignment`, `## Coding-standard alignment`, `## UI-specification compliance` (walk the ui-specification.md sections explicitly), `## i18n coverage`, `## Findings`, `## Verdict`.\n- R79 — contract gate Extension ↔ Daemon. Required headings: `## Contract surfaces`, `## Round-trip evidence`, `## Schema surfaces`, `## Findings`, `## Verdict`. New file `extension/src/test/contract.test.ts`.\n- T80 — large-repo performance tests: fixtures from T66, P99 budgets from Phases 1 and 2 verified at scale.\n- T81 — concurrency tests: parallel sessions, write contention, replay-safe execution.\n- T82 — recovery + corruption: corrupted event payloads, partial snapshots, replay-from-snapshot.\n- T83 — partial-index handling + workspace-boundary tests (per spec §Non-Negotiable Product Properties \"no silent broad workspace reads\").\n- T84 — migration tests + MCP schema compatibility regression (covers backward-compat shims from R64).\n- T85 — documentation suite. Required docs from spec §Documentation Requirements:\n  - successor architecture overview\n  - MCP contract reference (was T61)\n  - memory model reference\n  - event log design\n  - consolidation design\n  - retrieval/ranking design\n  - verification/freshness design\n  - operator guide\n  - migration guide from Lattice\n  - benchmark/evaluation guide\n  - extension review UI guide\n- T86 — operator runbook + recovery playbook. Includes deploy sequence: `pkill -f lattice && cp daemon/target/release/lattice extension/bin/ && cp daemon/target/release/lattice ~/.vscode/extensions/lattice.lattice-0.1.0/bin/` from `lattice/CLAUDE.md` Build/Deploy. Includes replay-from-snapshot procedure.\n- R87 — Phase 11 review. Required headings: `## Spec alignment`, `## Coding-standard alignment`, `## Doc coverage matrix` (one row per required doc from spec §Documentation Requirements), `## Hardening evidence`, `## Findings`, `## Verdict`.\n- R88 — definition-of-done gate. Required headings (one per checklist section from `shared/templates/definition-of-done-checklist.md`):\n  - `## Workflow Completion`\n  - `## Failure Handling`\n  - `## Security, Tenancy, and Audit`\n  - `## Data Integrity and Workflow Controls`\n  - `## Observability and Recovery`\n  - `## Performance and Scale`\n  - `## Documentation and Operator Readiness`\n  - `## Verification Evidence`\n  - `## Explicit Deferrals` — this MUST be either empty (no deferrals) or list each deferral with reason + owner + target date per the execution philosophy in `/home/pete/.claude/CLAUDE.md`. No silent deferrals.\n- R89 — final readiness review. Required headings:\n  - `## Spec coverage matrix` — one row per spec §Phase, status PASS/PASS-WITH-CAVEATS/BLOCK.\n  - `## Measurable success criteria` — one row per target from spec §Me